{"title":"Combined feed","url":"https://wulouniu.github.io/feeds/all.xml","elements":[{"title":"Bombay sandwich (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that the <b><a href=\"/wiki/Bombay_sandwich\" title=\"Bombay sandwich\">Bombay sandwich</a></b> <i>(example pictured)</i> typically uses potatoes and chutney, but some versions use chocolate?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bombay_sandwich","retrieved":1770619227073},{"title":"chaplains awarded the Medal of Honor (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that all five <b><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_Chaplain_Corps_Medal_of_Honor_recipients\" title=\"List of Chaplain Corps Medal of Honor recipients\">chaplains awarded the Medal of Honor</a></b> since the American Civil War were Catholic priests?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Chaplain_Corps_Medal_of_Honor_recipients","retrieved":1770619227074},{"title":"last person executed by Peru (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that the attorney of the <b><a href=\"/wiki/Julio_Vargas_Garayar\" title=\"Julio Vargas Garayar\">last person executed by Peru</a></b> requested Pope John Paul&nbsp;II's intervention to save his client's life?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julio_Vargas_Garayar","retrieved":1770619227075},{"title":"Cyclone Dana (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that mangroves reduced the impact of <b><a href=\"/wiki/Cyclone_Dana\" title=\"Cyclone Dana\">Cyclone Dana</a></b>?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyclone_Dana","retrieved":1770619227076},{"title":"Trisha Ziff (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that <i>Variety</i> once called <b><a href=\"/wiki/Trisha_Ziff\" title=\"Trisha Ziff\">Trisha Ziff</a></b> a \"photographer's photographer\"?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trisha_Ziff","retrieved":1770619227078},{"title":"16th Mechanized Infantry Brigade (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that the headquarters of Indonesia's <b><a href=\"/wiki/16th_Mechanized_Infantry_Brigade_(Indonesia)\" title=\"16th Mechanized Infantry Brigade (Indonesia)\">16th Mechanized Infantry Brigade</a></b> was a Japanese military base, seized by Indonesian youths after Japan's surrender in 1945?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/16th_Mechanized_Infantry_Brigade_(Indonesia)","retrieved":1770619227080},{"title":"four sea delicacies (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that <a href=\"/wiki/Shark_fin_soup\" title=\"Shark fin soup\">shark fin</a> is one of the \"<b><a href=\"/wiki/Four_sea_delicacies\" title=\"Four sea delicacies\">four sea delicacies</a></b>\", a quartet of luxury seafoods in Chinese cuisine?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_sea_delicacies","retrieved":1770619227082},{"title":"Immanuel Iheanacho (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that <b><a href=\"/wiki/Immanuel_Iheanacho\" title=\"Immanuel Iheanacho\">Immanuel Iheanacho</a></b> was measured as a 14-year-old freshman at 6&nbsp;ft 6&nbsp;in (1.98&nbsp;m) and 325&nbsp;lb (147&nbsp;kg), with a 7&nbsp;ft (2.1&nbsp;m) <a href=\"/wiki/Arm_span\" title=\"Arm span\">wingspan</a>?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immanuel_Iheanacho","retrieved":1770619227087},{"title":"Mecki (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that in 1956 a person dressed as the anthropomorphic hedgehog and comic star <b><a href=\"/wiki/Mecki\" title=\"Mecki\">Mecki</a></b> traveled by helicopter to more than 100 cities in southern Germany to give children gifts?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mecki","retrieved":1770619227088},{"title":"Destination of the Month (Wikivoyage recommendations)","contents":"<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r4523569\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt7\" id=\"mwIQ\" data-mw=\"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Banner/styles.css&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;banner&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Banner&